The plan is written: two tasks in session_plan/, both on #1142, the yoagent 0.26 → 0.27.1 upgrade the creator asked for. The commit step failed because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the files exist on disk but nothing was committed. The instruction's || true suggests that's expected.

`task_01.md`: Part of #1142 (bump the version and re-read every claim)
• Set yoagent to "0.27" and move the lock to 0.27.1. Tonight's probe compiled cleanly under 0.27; cargo test hasn't been run against it yet.
• This task touches more than 3 files, on purpose. tests/doc_version_claims.rs fails on all 34 0.26 markers as soon as the lock moves, so the bump and the marker re-read can't be split without leaving the tree red in between. Everything outside Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, image_cap.rs and output_limit.rs is a comment edit.
• What gets re-read is everything the 0.27 changes touch in my tree, not only the 34 marked paragraphs. Two claims are already known to be false:
  • Image cap: src/image_cap.rs says its 20 MB cap matches yoagent's. At 0.27.1 yoagent sends only PNG, JPEG and WebP, up to 3.75 MB. The task makes the cap read yoagent::tools::DEFAULT_MAX_IMAGE_BYTES instead of a typed number, with tests exactly at the limit and one byte over.
  • `on_stop`: the comment in src/prompt/output_limit.rs says on_stop isn't called when an answer hits the output limit. Since 0.27.0 it is.
• It also warns about two files close to the size limit: src/config.rs is 11 lines away and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs 14.

`task_02.md`: Fixes #1142 and #1138
• Startup certificate check: the task first measures what yoagent 0.27.1 actually prints when the certificate setting is bad. The default is to keep my check, because it refuses before any prompt is sent and names the variable. It gets dropped only if yoagent's message turns out to arrive as early and name the variable too. The reason goes into the module doc.
• Crash message: when the agent task panics, yoyo currently says "reply cut off". The task gives a crash its own message and a non-zero exit code. It's tested on the function that decides which message to show, not just on the text.
• Old pointers: every #1138 mention in src/ and docs/ gets updated, since this push closes that issue.

